                <mxCell id="ev" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;" value="&lt;b&gt;BATCH EVAL  (RAGAS-style)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&#39;font-size:10px&#39;&gt;fixed test set + sampled traces + 👍/👎&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&#39;font-size:10px&#39;&gt;→ scores in Postgres → dashboard&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&#39;font-size:10px&#39;&gt;tracks quality release to release&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="90" width="300" x="2480" y="1840" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="g_notes" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#333333;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=4;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#333333;" value="KEY CHANGES vs v1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="170" width="820" x="-110" y="1900" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;" value="1. Caches are checked before retrieval (v1: after reranking), so a hit skips search and the cross-encoder.&lt;br&gt;2. Redis exact-match is checked before FAISS semantic (cheap check first). Cache keys include filters and user scope.&lt;br&gt;3. The input guardrail runs first, so unsafe queries cost nothing downstream.&lt;br&gt;4. Eval results go to Postgres, never back into the ingestion corpus, so model outputs can&#39;t be retrieved as evidence.&lt;br&gt;5. New: Postgres, API gateway, rate limits, sessions, LLM gateway, model router, observability, offline eval.&lt;br&gt;6. LLM is API-only (no self-hosted inference). Embeddings, CLIP and the cross-encoder still run on your own server." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="130" width="795" x="-95" y="1930" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>